e formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'specialized password database formats' is subjective and undefined, and 'File formats' does not clarify which formats are being referenced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-028\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats are not specialized password database formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the scope boundary specifying which file formats or operations (e.g., import/export formats vs. native database files) this requirement applies to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-028\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats are not specialized password database formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Unconditionally asserts that file formats are not specialized password database formats, conflicting with KP-003, which mandates a specialized '.kdb' database file format.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"low-level layout\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'low-level layout' is vague and untestable without concrete format definitions or criteria, and 'File formats' does not specify which formats are meant.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-029\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats only specify a low-level layout of stored data\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the scope specifying which file formats or operations (e.g., import/export vs. database storage) are covered and omits concrete format specifications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-030\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Global hot key cannot be changed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not define which key combination constitutes the 'Global hot key' or what action it triggers, uses passive voice ('cannot be changed') without naming the actor, and omits behavior if a change is attempted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-031\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Title, username or URL cannot be changed in a TAN entry.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a field-modification restriction without specifying how the system enforces or handles attempted edits (e.g., read-only fields or error feedback), uses passive voice without naming the actor, and leaves 'TAN' undefined.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-032\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When a TAN is used\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'used' is ambiguous because it does not define what action constitutes using a TAN (e.g., viewing, copying to clipboard, auto-typing, or manually marking as used).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When a TAN is used, it expires automatically and can never be used again.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the concrete system behavior or state change upon expiration (e.g., deleting, marking expired, or disabling copy/auto-type) or how the system responds if a user attempts to reuse an expired TAN.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":293.98729,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":14306,"output_tokens":33321,"thinking_tokens":28440,"cache_read_tokens":12119,"total_tokens":47627}}}
